# Python bytecode from tools/artwork/. The importer itself is committed (it is how authored and
# contributed art is converted to the TGA the client loads); its compiled cache is not.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Machine-local state from tools/artwork/wiki_import.py. The manifest itself IS committed — it is
# the reviewed record of which source becomes which permanent catalog id — but these two are not:
#
#   .root    the absolute path of whoever's download directory the manifest was scaffolded from.
#   .stamps  what each output was last built from, so an edited erase box or a changed --size
#            reconverts instead of being skipped as up to date. Rebuildable, and meaningless on
#            another machine.
#
# .tmp is the atomic-write staging file for both; it exists only mid-write.
tools/artwork/manifest.tsv.root
tools/artwork/.stamps.tsv
tools/artwork/*.tmp
